{
  "table_id": "Table_S24",
  "display_number": "S24",
  "title": "Supplementary Table S24. Primary continuous-exposure models: per-IQR associations of EVI and O₃ with BAA across scales and specifications.",
  "panel": "",
  "panel_title": "",
  "notes_before": [],
  "notes_after": [
    "Note. Estimates are adjusted BAA differences (years) per interquartile-range increase in 4-year mean exposure from linear mixed-effects models with participant-level random intercepts and robust (sandwich) variance (N = 5,914 observations from 3,154 participants). Single-exposure models include one exposure; dual-exposure models mutually adjust EVI and O₃. The unweighted dual-exposure 1-km rows are the prespecified primary analysis (main-text Figure 2); both primary tests remained significant after Benjamini-Hochberg correction. IQRs: EVI 0.053 (1 km) and 0.048 (500 m); O₃ 6.8 and 7.3 μg m⁻³. Abbreviations: BAA, biological age acceleration; CI, confidence interval; EVI, enhanced vegetation index; IPW, inverse-probability weighting; IQR, interquartile range; O₃, ozone."
  ],
